  home_card_kontakt_text: "Address, phone number and directions.",

  leitbild_title_page: "Mission - Rägiräupli Playgroup",
  leitbild_title: "Our Mission",
  leitbild_p1: "In our playgroup, the child is at the centre of everything we do.",
  leitbild_p2: "Every child is unique and brings their own needs, abilities and pace. We offer a safe space where children can feel comfortable, explore and grow.",
  leitbild_p3: "Through free play and a variety of activities, we help children experience the world in a playful way, using all their senses. In doing so, we encourage their curiosity, creativity and joy in doing things together.",
  leitbild_p4: "A key part of our work is social interaction. Children learn to find their place within the group, to be considerate of others, to build friendships and to resolve early conflicts in an age-appropriate way.",
  leitbild_p5: "We accompany children with empathy on their path towards independence. Gentle transitions, trust and security form the foundation for healthy development.",
  leitbild_p6: "Every child is free to grow and develop with us – at their own pace. We meet children with appreciation, patience and respect.",
  leitbild_p7: "A trusting partnership with parents is very important to us. Together, we create an environment in which children feel secure and can develop as a whole person.",

  konzept_title_page: "Concept - Rägiräupli Playgroup",
  konzept_title: "Our Concept",
  konzept_einleitung_h: "Introduction",
  konzept_einleitung_p1: "This pedagogical concept forms the basis for the work of the Rägiräupli Playgroup. Our goal is to support children holistically in their individual development and to offer them a safe space for their first social experiences outside the family.",
  konzept_einleitung_p2: "Our work is based on a resource-oriented and appreciative approach. Each child is seen as an individual personality with their own strengths, interests and stages of development. We focus on the needs of the children and create an environment in which they feel safe, accepted and taken seriously.",
  konzept_einleitung_p3: "The playgroup sees itself as a place for free play, shared experiences and social learning, with learning through experience and relationships at its heart.",
  konzept_grundsaetze_h: "Principles and Goals",
  konzept_grundsaetze_p1: "The Rägiräupli Playgroup supports children in their social, emotional, cognitive, physical and psychological development. Our goals are:",
  konzept_grundsaetze_li1: "Fostering social skills (e.g. sharing, consideration for others, conflict resolution)",
  konzept_grundsaetze_li2: "Strengthening self-competence (self-confidence, independence, tolerance for frustration)",
  konzept_grundsaetze_li3: "Developing practical skills (curiosity, creative thinking, problem-solving ability)",
  konzept_grundsaetze_li4: "Fostering learning skills (perseverance, concentration, joy of discovery)",
  konzept_grundsaetze_p2: "We offer children space for free play, creative activities, movement, singing together, listening to stories, and themed activities.",
  konzept_grundsaetze_p3: "Our pedagogical approach is shaped by appreciation, patience, clarity and reliability. We accompany children mindfully and give them a sense of direction through clear structures and rituals.",
  konzept_haltung_h: "Our Approach",
  konzept_haltung_p1: "We meet children at eye level and take their feelings, needs and ideas seriously. A relationship of trust forms the basis of our work.",
  konzept_haltung_p2: "We see ourselves as companions who provide encouragement, convey security and strengthen children's independence. We give children time – time to arrive, to try things out, to learn and to grow.",
  konzept_haltung_p3: "Rules and boundaries provide guidance and security. They are communicated clearly and applied consistently, but always with kindness.",
  konzept_alltag_h: "A Day at the Playgroup",
  konzept_alltag_p1: "A playgroup session is clearly structured while still leaving enough room for individual play. Typical routine:",
  konzept_alltag_li1: "Arrival and greeting",
  konzept_alltag_li2: "Free play",
  konzept_alltag_li3: "Group activity (e.g. crafts, singing, movement games, stories)",
  konzept_alltag_li4: "Snack time (Znüni/Zvieri) – prepared together",
  konzept_alltag_li5: "Closing circle ritual",
  konzept_alltag_p2: "Rituals give children a sense of security and orientation in everyday life.",
  konzept_alltag_p3: "We provide a wide variety of play materials: building and construction materials, a role-play corner, books, creative materials, natural materials, etc. These materials stimulate imagination, creativity and independent action.",
  konzept_alltag_p4: "In everyday life, we support children through:",
  konzept_alltag_li6: "Encouragement and positive feedback",
  konzept_alltag_li7: "Support during conflicts",
  konzept_alltag_li8: "Fostering independence (e.g. getting dressed, tidying up)",
  konzept_alltag_li9: "Language as a key means of guidance",
  konzept_raeume_h: "Our Premises",
  konzept_raeume_p1: "The playgroup has bright, child-friendly and safely furnished rooms. Different play areas allow for a wide range of experiences (movement area, creative corner, role-play corner, building area, etc.).",
  konzept_raeume_p2: "Whenever possible, we make regular use of our back yard. Movement and experiences in nature are an important part of our work.",
  konzept_gallery_exterior_alt: "Rägiräupli Playgroup seen from outside",
  konzept_gallery_interior_alt: "Playroom of the Rägiräupli Playgroup",
  konzept_eltern_h: "Working with Parents",
  konzept_eltern_p1: "A trusting and open partnership with parents is very important to us. It forms the basis for the child's wellbeing. Exchange takes place:",
  konzept_eltern_li1: "through brief conversations when dropping off and picking up",
  konzept_eltern_li2: "through scheduled parent meetings when needed",
  konzept_eltern_li3: "by e-mail or phone",
  konzept_eltern_li4: "through parents' evenings, where applicable",
  konzept_eltern_p2: "We take parents' requests for conversations seriously and arrange an appointment promptly. We maintain open, respectful and transparent communication.",
  konzept_events_h: "Events with Parents",
  konzept_events_infoabend_h: "Information Evening",
  konzept_events_infoabend_p: "Every year in August.",
  konzept_events_samichlaus_h: "St. Nicholas",
  konzept_events_samichlaus_p: "A visit from St. Nicholas at the playgroup.",
  konzept_events_ostern_h: "Easter Egg Hunt",
  konzept_events_ostern_p: "A shared Easter celebration with the families.",

